==============================================================================
  9. An honest finding   (~1 min)
  Syllabus topic: distributed measurement, clocks
==============================================================================
  SAY:
   - On RDS our sync-lag view showed NEGATIVE latency: a change arriving before it was made.
   - Cause: the lag compared the laptop's clock with the RDS server's clock, and they differed by ~1.5 s.
   - Fix: measure both ends on one clock. Lesson: distributed timings need a single clock.
    PG_DSN: rtt 19.6 ms, server clock minus local clock -1489.4 ms
    DOCKER_PG_DSN: rtt 1.1 ms, server clock minus local clock -0.9 ms
  SAY:
   - Thank you. Questions?
